From: Fedora macchanger maintainers <macchanger-maintainers@fedoraproject.org>
Date: Fri, 4 Jul 2014 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] warnings: check seed read and print size_t portably

Require a complete random-seed read before accepting it, retain the existing
time/PID fallback, and use %zu for strlen()'s size_t result. These fixes are
carried by Fedora 44 for macchanger 1.7.0 and avoid architecture-sensitive
format diagnostics.

Root cause: upstream 1.7.0 ignores a possibly short read and prints size_t
through a long-unsigned format that is not portable across data models.
Patch-Source: Fedora 44 macchanger-1.7.0-30.fc44 source RPM,
              macchanger-1.7.0-werror.diff
Patch-License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (existing Fedora downstream patch)
Removal: remove when a stable upstream release validates the seed read and
         uses a size_t-compatible diagnostic format.

---
 src/mac.c  | 2 +-
 src/main.c | 8 ++++++--
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/main.c b/src/main.c
--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -96,0 +97 @@
+	int            have_seed = 0;
@@ -101 +102 @@
-		read (fd, &seed, sizeof(seed));
+		have_seed = (read (fd, &seed, sizeof(seed)) == sizeof(seed));
@@ -103 +104,4 @@
-	} else {
+	}
+
+	/* Use a predictable non-constant seed as a fallback. */
+	if (!have_seed) {
diff --git a/src/mac.c b/src/mac.c
--- a/src/mac.c
+++ b/src/mac.c
@@ -116 +116 @@
-		fprintf (stderr, "[ERROR] Incorrect format: MAC length should be 17. %s(%lu)\n", string, strlen(string));
+		fprintf (stderr, "[ERROR] Incorrect format: MAC length should be 17. %s(%zu)\n", string, strlen(string));
--
2.50.1
